{
 "id": "lighting.natural",
 "label": "Natural light",
 "description": "Named sunlight, skylight, window light, twilight, moonlight, and weather-shaped natural lighting looks.",
 "pos": "noun phrase",
 "frame": "lit by ___",
 "notes": "Named natural illumination belongs here, phrased to follow “lit by.” lighting.indoor_practical owns flames and visible fixtures; lighting.studio owns photographic setups, and lighting.dramatic owns designed cinematic effects. Time-of-day, space, and climate tags keep each look tied to compatible conditions. The space tag is the setting a look needs: window sources need an indoor subject, sky and sun looks an outdoor one (or either, for sunlight through a window), underwater sunlight an underwater scene; such a look is drawn only once the prompt or a drawn place states that setting (context.takes.space.unstated), and soft natural light and bright natural daylight need none. Looks that place the scene somewhere more specific than its space (ice caves, auroras, canyons, snowfields, beaches, mountains, forests, an eclipse) are opt-in: drawn only when the prompt's words or the user ask for them. The two golden-hour entries distinguish broad warmth from low raking light.",
 "facets": [
  "space",
  "time_of_day",
  "climate"
 ],
